3.text:
PRIVATE REFLECTION: The board is treated as a local corner with no edge limit, so D1–D2 is not in atari and White is not forced to play D3. The three Black complexes are

* G_A = {A2}  L = {A1,A3,B2}
* G_B = {B3,B4}  L = {A3,A4,B2}
* G_C = {C1,C2}  L = {B1,B2}

B2 is the unique point that joins the three complexes and B1 is the unique atari point of G_C.  Occupying any of the five liberty points A1,A3,A4,B1,B2 removes one liberty from at least two of the complexes and creates a mutual atari on the White stone that is played.  In each case Black’s only saving replies are B2 or B1, and after the forced reply the remaining Black material is reduced to the two-point set {A1,A4} together with the mutual atari on B1.  The subsequent White A3/A4 net then fills the last liberties and the whole A2-B3-B4-C1-C2 army is captured.  In particular

1.W B1 2.B B2 forces W A3/A4 and the net,
1.W B2 2.B B1 forces W A3/A4 and the net,

and the same net is obtained by the symmetric first plays A1, A3 and A4 which all reduce the combined liberties of G_A∪G_B∪G_C to the {A1,A4,B1} miai.  Hence the five liberty points of the Black shape can all be used to initiate a forced kill, the usual textbook first moves being B1 and B2.

