3.text:
{A1,A3,A4,B1,B2}

The right hand White net is not in immediate atari, L(D1–D2)={E1,E2,D3}, so White is not forced to play D3 first.

The three Black complexes are

Ga = A2        L(Ga) = {A1,A3,B2}
Gb = B3–B4      L(Gb) = {A3,A4,B2}
Gc = C1–C2      L(Gc) = {B1,B2}

They are tied on the five shared liberties {A1,A3,A4,B1,B2}. Occupying any one of them removes a liberty from ≥2 complexes and puts the White stone into a mutual atari with the net.

* 1.W B1 → 2.B B2 forced else Gc falls. Merged A2–B2–B3–B4–C1–C2 has L={A1,A3,A4} with W B1 in atari on A1. 3.W A3/A4 4.B A1 captures B1 5.W A4/A3 finishes the A1–A3–A4 miai.
* 1.W B2 → L(Gc)={B1}, L(Ga)={A1,A3}, L(Gb)={A3,A4}. 2.B B1 forced else W B1 captures Gc. B1–C1–C2 is 1-liberty on A1, 3.W A1 captures it and Ga/Gb is left on the A3/A4 miai.
* 1.W A1, 1.W A3, 1.W A4 are transpositions of the same net. After the forced connection B2/B1 the three complexes merge to {A3,A4,B1} / {A1,A4,B1} / {A1,A3,B1} with the White attacking stone in mutual atari, and the subsequent A3/A4/B1 squeeze removes the last liberties of the merged A2–B3–B4–C1–C2 mass.

Any first move outside {A1,A3,A4,B1,B2} leaves Black a connecting/defending reply that keeps the three complexes alive. Up to the usual sacrifice of D1–D2 the five shared-liberty points are the killing initiators.

